/*!
 * \file mfem-mgis.doxygen
 * \brief This file contains the main page of the doxygen
 * documentation and the documentation of the mfem_mgis namespace.
 */

/*!
 * \mainpage An introduction to the MFEM/MGIS project
 * \author   Thomas Helfer
 * \date     20/02/2025
 *
 * MFEM/MGIS is a C++ library for nonlinear thermo-mechanical simulations on
 * HPC systems, combining [`MFEM`](https://mfem.org/) finite elements and
 * [`MFront`](https://thelfer.github.io/tfel/web/index.html) behaviours
 * through [`MGIS`](https://github.com/thelfer/MFrontGenericInterfaceSupport).
 *
 * The goal and features of MFEM/MGIS are described in its
 * [JOSS paper](https://doi.org/10.21105/joss.07719).
 *
 * The MFEM/MGIS project documentation is available
 * [here](https://thelfer.github.io/mfem-mgis/).
 *
 * A tutorial based on a mechanical notched beam is given
 * [here](https://thelfer.github.io/mfem-mgis/user_guide/tutorial.html).
 *
 * Installation guidelines are available
 * [here](https://thelfer.github.io/mfem-mgis/installation_guide/installation_guide.html).
 *
 * Some examples of MFEM/MGIS use are stored in
 * [mfem-mgis-examples](https://github.com/latug0/mfem-mgis-examples) and
 * [mm-opera-hpc](https://github.com/rprat-pro/mm-opera-hpc).
 */

/*!
 * \namespace mfem_mgis
 * \brief the namespace mfem_mgis encloses all the MFEM/MGIS project.
 */
